From 89d6b60440cd977747f3ea9387e7d3c1c1c0cc3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vasilii Zolotukhin <vasilii.zolotukhin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 07:44:30 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Mac: join profile windows into one native window tab
 group

Normal browser windows of all profiles (incognito included) are added to
one NSWindow tab group with explicit -addTabbedWindow:ordered:; the
global allowsAutomaticWindowTabbing stays off. Each system tab is titled
with the profile name from ProfileAttributesStorage ("Name (Incognito)",
"Name 2" for extra windows) and follows profile renames. DevTools,
popups, app windows and windows torn off a tab strip are left alone.

While a window shows the native tab bar, the browser UI moves below the
standard titlebar and the tab bar ("profile tabs on top"); fullscreen
keeps Chromium's own layout.

All logic lives in profile_tabs_mac.{h,mm}; existing files only get
short hooks in BrowserNativeWidgetMac and BrowserFrameViewMac.
